restrictions:
  - "Alignment: any. The book says Sand Dragons tend to be Scrupulous (20%), Unprincipled (25%) or Anarchist (30%)."
  - "Speed: 3D6+6 running, and 3D6+30 swimming (averaging 30 mph/48 km or 26 knots)."
  - "Attacks per melee: four physical attacks per melee round, or two by magic."
  - "The +1 on Perception Rolls becomes +2 on anything involving building."
  - "+1 on all saving throws other than Horror Factor (which is +2)."
  - "Prowl is +10% in sand and water only."
  - "VULNERABILITIES: cold attacks do double damage. It hates dark, ugly places, and trapped in one it becomes depressed: -1 attack per melee, no Perception Roll or initiative bonuses, -20% on skill performance, -1 on all combat moves, and Spd reduced by 20%."
  - "MAGIC: born with a full understanding of magic but knows NO spells at level one. It can learn magic, and can use Techno-Wizard, Biomancy and other magical weapons and devices. Under the Rifts Ultimate Edition hatchling rules the book points to (p.158), spells are learned by the usual means from second level - by third level the hatchling has 2D4+2 spells from levels 1-3, another 2D4+2 by fifth level from levels 3-8, and 3 new spells per level thereafter up to its own level. Two spells may be cast per melee round, and it gains +1 to spell strength at level nine. Those counts are dice-valued, which a spell schedule cannot hold, so they are recorded here."
  - "PSIONICS: a Master Psychic. Empathy and Object Read, plus five powers of choice all taken from ONE of the Healing or Sensitive categories. One new power from that same category at each new level of experience, and Telemechanics at level 6."
  - "On S.D.C. worlds a hatchling has 220 Hit Points, 2D6x10+30 S.D.C. and a Natural A.R. of 11 in place of its M.D.C."
  - "Size: an adult is 20-30 feet (6.1 to 9.1 m) from snout to rump, plus 30-40 feet (9.1 to 12.2 m) of tail, and weighs 18-30 tons. The book prints no separate hatchling size."
  - "It takes criticism of its sand castles and sculptures badly, and is easily offended even by a well-meant suggestion."
  - "From Rifts Ultimate Edition p.158, Magic Knowledge: without being taught it can work any Techno-Wizard device, recognise and use other magic weapons, read magic and use scrolls, and it recognises magic circles and enchantment at 40% +3% per level of experience. It senses ley lines and nexus points within 20 miles (32 km), and other dragons - even ones disguised by metamorphosis - on sight out to 4000 feet (1219 m). The sensing gives nearness and general direction, never an exact spot."
  - "From Rifts Ultimate Edition p.158, Weapons and Equipment: it can use any kind of weapon, and wears little clothing or mega-damage armor except as a disguise in humanoid form. It mostly counts on what it was born with, its magic and its psionics."
  - "From the Rifts Ultimate Edition hatchling rules (p.156-159) the book defers to: a hatchling behaves like a child of four to seven and must settle on a definitive alignment at level three; it does not need to eat or drink; it can never take cybernetics or bionics, which its bio-regeneration pushes back out; and under 100 years old it cares little for wealth, though it is always drawn to magic items."
side_effects: "ADULT SAND DRAGON (not playable; the class stores the hatchling). Attributes I.Q. 2D6+12, M.E. 2D6+15, M.A. 2D6+12, P.S. 2D6+26, P.P. 2D6+10, P.E. 3D6+10, P.B. 3D6+7, Spd 3D6+38 running (around 35 mph/56 km) and 4D6+60 swimming (averaging 50 mph/80 km or 43 knots). M.D.C. 1D6x1,000+1,200, +1D4x1,000 for an ancient (S.D.C. worlds: 5D6x10+120 Hit Points, 2D6x100 S.D.C., Natural A.R. 15). Horror Factor 13. P.P.E. 1D6x100+400. I.S.P. 3D6x10 + M.E., +10 per level; all Sensitive or all Healing powers plus Hydrokinesis, Telemechanics and Telemechanic Mental Operation. Six physical attacks per melee, or three by magic. +4 on Perception Rolls, +2 initiative, +3 strike and parry, +2 dodge (+4 automatic dodge underwater), +6 pull punch, +3 roll with impact, +4 vs Horror Factor, +2 on all other saves. Magic: one of Ocean Magic (25%), Wizard/Spell Invocations as a Ley Line Walker (25%), Earth Warlock Magic (30%) or Temporal Magic (20%), about 2D6+14 spells; it avoids dark magic such as Necromancy. Life span 1D6x1,000+2,000 years, some reaching 10,000. NPC level: 2D4 for adults, 1D4 for hatchlings."
extraction_notes: |
  Read from Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria printed 219-220 (cache p220-p221;
  cache page = printed + 1). Neither cache page is flagged for digit swaps;
  the stat block, bonuses and psionics were still checked against 170-dpi
  renders. The text layer on printed 220 runs its paragraphs out of order.

  Section heading: "Sea Dragons" (printed 208). A race, so no men_of_arms
  line is needed: the class states mdc_base.

  WHAT THE BOOK DEFERS TO RIFTS ULTIMATE EDITION, AND WHAT WAS REUSED.
  The entry says "Hatchling player characters start at level one" and twice
  sends the reader to Rifts Ultimate Edition p.156 for playing a dragon
  hatchling. Taken from the published dragon-hatchling-flame-wind class, not
  from this book:
  1. xp_table - the Rifts Ultimate Edition dragon ladder, copied from
     dragon-hatchling-flame-wind. This entry prints no ladder; the Leviathan
     in the same section (printed 209-210) says to use the Dragon Experience
     Table. Rifts Ultimate Edition''s Experience Tables (printed 295) head
     this ladder "Dragon Hatchling & Adult Dragon", and its hatchling
     section (printed 158) says to use the Dragon R.C.C. for level
     advancement.
  2. The spell-learning progression in the MAGIC restriction, and the last
     restriction line (alignment at level three, no need to eat, no
     cybernetics, money). This book prints only "know no spells at Level
     One ... can learn magic and use Techno-Wizard, Biomancy and other magical
     weapons and devices".
  3. The Magic Knowledge and Weapons and Equipment restriction lines, and
     "two spells per melee round, +1 to spell strength at level nine" in the
     MAGIC line. Rifts Ultimate Edition printed 158 prints all three in its
     general Dragon Hatchling section, as rules for every hatchling (the
     cache prints the spell strength figure as "+f"; it is +1).
  NOT reused: Rifts Ultimate Edition''s skill scheme (instinctive skills at
  98%, Secondary Skills, Special Areas of Interest). This entry prints its own
  "R.C.C. Skills (Hatchling)" list, which is what is stored.

  WHAT THE BOOK PRINTS AND WHAT WAS STORED.
  1. Skills: 17 named skills with a printed bonus; each base is the catalog
     base plus that bonus. "Pilot: Sail Boats" is held as Boat: Sail Type,
     "Pilot: Water Skiing and Surfing" as Water Skiing & Surfing, "Underwater
     Navigation" as Navigation: Underwater, "General Repair and Maintenance"
     as General Repair & Maintenance, "Military Fortifications" as Military
     Fortification, "Whittling and Sculpting" as Whittling & Sculpting,
     "Literate in Dragonese/Elven" as Literacy: Dragonese/Elven.
  2. "Prowl (+10% in sand and water only)" is conditional: Prowl is stored at
     the catalog''s 25% and the +10% is prose.
  3. "A total of four skill selections from ... Aquatic, Communication,
     Domestic, Science, Technical and Wilderness" is stored as a
     four-pick choice group in occ_skills with bonus 0. The catalog has no Aquatic category:
     the book''s Aquatic Skills list (printed 54) is spread over Technical,
     Wilderness, Science, Horsemanship, Medical and Pilot Related, so
     Horsemanship and Medical are named with `only` lists holding the
     Aquatic skills filed there. Left out: Horsemanship: Serpent Hunter (the Serpent
     Hunter''s own) and Navigation: Underwater (Pilot Related; already an
     R.C.C. skill here). A single { name: "Aquatic", only: [...] } entry was
     tested and is refused by categoryAllows: a cross-category `only` is
     admitted only when the group also lists the skill''s real category.
  4. "Magically understands and speaks all languages at 90%" is stored as
     Language: All (magical) at 90 with no per-level gain.
  5. Attacks: "Four physical or two by magic" is stored as attacks_base 4.
  6. "+1 on all other saving throws" is stored as +1 on each of the fourteen
     other d20 saves the sheet draws (the percentile coma/death save is left
     alone), following dragon-hatchling-asama-tatsu, and is also kept as a
     restriction line.
  7. Perception +1 is stored; "(+2 to anything involving building)" is prose.
  8. Horror Factor 10 is stored in horror_factor.
  9. The S.D.C.-world figures (220 Hit Points, 2D6x10+30 S.D.C.) are stored in
     hit_points_base and sdc_base as the flame-wind model does; Natural A.R.
     11 is prose.
  10. Psionics: "five of choice selected either from Healing or Sensitive
      categories (pick one)" is stored as five picks across both categories,
      with the one-category rule in prose - nothing holds a pick to the
      category chosen first. One power per new level is written as a schedule
      entry per level, because a level-6 entry for Telemechanics is needed
      beside it. Telemechanics is a Super power; the level-6 entry names it
      outright. "Object Read" is held as Object Read (Psychometry).
  11. Spd stores the running figure (3D6+6); swimming Spd 3D6+30 is prose.
  12. Adult and ancient figures are prose only (side_effects). The adult''s
      "Telemechanics Mental Operation" is the catalog''s Telemechanic Mental
      Operation.

  BOOK SLIPS.
  - Printed 219: the alignment percentages sum to 75%.
  - Printed 220: Mega-Damage and the natural abilities do not separate adult
    from hatchling, and the breath weapon prints one figure (3D6 M.D.) for
    both. Stored once, as printed.
