## Lore

Sand Dragons are pale creatures - bone white through cream to gold - with a
green or red frill around the neck and a matching line of fins down the spine.
They are builders. A young one starts with small castles and figures on a
beach, and the habit grows with the dragon until it is raising whole palaces
of sand, silt and sea-floor rubble, on dry land or under the waves, bound
together by its own magic. Wind and tide pull most of them down again, and
the dragon is perfectly happy to start over.

They are among the calmest dragons known. They would rather think, talk with
anyone who will talk, explore and look at art and scenery than fight, and
they are as content on a desert or a beach as in the deep ocean. They are
also newcomers: experienced travelers between dimensions who have only lately
reached Rifts Earth, owe nobody here anything, and are puzzled by how much of
the planet seems to be at war. They like Lemurians best, without quite
understanding the Lemurians'' war either.

They dislike cold and darkness, and they do not take criticism of their work
well.

## GM Notes

A Sand Dragon hatchling is the gentlest of the four sea dragons to put in a
party: modest combat bonuses, a blinding breath weapon rather than a killing
one, and a signature ability that builds things. Build with and Fortify Sand
costs 25 P.P.E. per 12 foot section, which a hatchling''s pool covers only a
few times over, so anything large is a project for a ley line.

Its weaknesses are cold, which does double damage, and confinement somewhere
dark and ugly, which strips its Perception and initiative bonuses and costs
it an attack. Other dragons of darkness and most of Lemuria''s enemies dislike
it on sight.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-hatchling-sand');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-hatchling-sand';

